# AgencyOS — environment variables
#
# Setup:   cp .env.example .env.local   and fill in the values below.
# .env.local is gitignored. Never commit real keys.
#
# Every variable here is validated at boot by src/lib/env.ts. A missing or
# malformed value fails fast with a readable message rather than surfacing as a
# confusing runtime error later.

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# SUPABASE  —  required for Feature 1
#
# Create a project at https://supabase.com/dashboard (region: ap-south-1 /
# Mumbai), then find these under:  Project Settings → API Keys
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# "Project URL". Format: https://<project-ref>.supabase.co
NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_URL=

# Publishable key — "sb_publishable_..."
# (older projects call this the anon / public key, a long "eyJ..." JWT)
# Safe to expose to the browser: it is powerless without a Row Level Security
# policy that grants access.
NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=

# Secret key — "sb_secret_..."  (older projects: the service_role JWT)
# ⚠️ BYPASSES ROW LEVEL SECURITY. Server-only, never sent to the browser.
# Used in exactly four places (ARCHITECTURE.md §7.3): cron handlers, webhook
# handlers, the job runner, and migration scripts.
SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY=

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# APPLICATION
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

NEXT_PUBLIC_APP_URL=http://localhost:3000

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# JOB RUNNER  —  required for Feature 6 (AI Requirement Collection)
#
# Shared secret authenticating POST /api/jobs/run, the only place the
# service-role client may execute an agent run (ARCHITECTURE.md §7.3).
#
# Leave unset and the runner returns 503 rather than running unauthenticated:
# a deployment that has not configured it is inert, not open. Minimum 16 chars.
#
#   openssl rand -hex 32
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

CRON_SECRET=

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# ANTHROPIC  —  required for Feature 6 (AI Requirement Collection)
#
# Read only by the Claude provider (src/lib/ai/claude.ts). The *model* is not
# configured here: it comes from ai.agents.default_model, so retargeting an
# agent is an UPDATE, not a deploy (ARCHITECTURE.md §6.7).
#
# Leave unset and the provider does not register — extraction fails with
# AI_PROVIDER_NOT_CONFIGURED and nothing else is affected.
#
#   https://platform.claude.com/settings/keys
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# SPEECH TO TEXT  —  optional, and ADM-94 is still open
#
# What it buys: a client's voice note becomes the words that are in it, so the
# sales agent answers what they said instead of an envelope. On WhatsApp in
# India that is most of the enquiry.
#
# Leave it unset and nothing pretends: the recording is recorded, the
# transcript reads `[voice note — not transcribed]`, and the client is still
# answered. That is the honest state rather than a broken one.
#
# ADM-94 asks the owner which service, on whose account. The adapter written
# is OpenAI's — argued on capability, because these recordings are
# Hindi/English code-switching — and a different vendor is one file plus one
# line in src/lib/ai/router.ts.
#
#   https://platform.openai.com/api-keys
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

OPENAI_API_KEY=

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# WHATSAPP (INBOUND)  —  required for Feature 7 (inbound lead capture)
#
# Both are read by GET/POST /api/webhooks/whatsapp. Leave either unset and the
# webhook answers 503 rather than accepting traffic it cannot authenticate: a
# deployment that has not configured it is inert, not open.
#
# These two are for RECEIVING only. Sending is a separate, human-gated step
# that does not exist yet (ARCHITECTURE.md §6.1: AI proposes, a human sends),
# so WHATSAPP_ACCESS_TOKEN and WHATSAPP_PHONE_NUMBER_ID are deliberately absent
# until there is code that would use them. The business number is NOT
# configured here either — an organization claims one by storing its
# phone_number_id in core.organizations.settings, so adding a second tenant is
# an UPDATE rather than a deploy.
#
#   Meta app dashboard → WhatsApp → Configuration
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# Chosen by you, then entered in the dashboard's "Verify token" field. Meta
# echoes it back during the subscription handshake. Minimum 16 chars.
#
#   openssl rand -hex 32
WHATSAPP_VERIFY_TOKEN=

# Meta app secret — App settings → Basic → App Secret.
# Verifies the X-Hub-Signature-256 HMAC on every delivery. Without it, anyone
# who knows the URL could post a message as any client.
WHATSAPP_APP_SECRET=

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# GOOGLE OAUTH  —  required for Feature 3 (internal staff sign-in)
#
# These are NOT read by the app. Supabase performs the OAuth exchange, so the
# credentials are configured in the dashboard, not here:
#   Authentication → Sign In / Providers → Google
#
# In Google Cloud Console, the authorised redirect URI must be:
#   https://<project-ref>.supabase.co/auth/v1/callback
#
# Listed for the record so the setup is discoverable from one place.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# NOT YET USED — added by later features. Left here as a map, not a TODO.
#
#   Feature 3 (Auth)          GOOGLE_CLIENT_ID, GOOGLE_CLIENT_SECRET
#   Feature 6 (AI)            OPENAI_API_KEY (embeddings only — §6.4),
#                             AI_DAILY_BUDGET_MINOR
#   Feature 7 (WhatsApp out)  WHATSAPP_ACCESS_TOKEN, WHATSAPP_PHONE_NUMBER_ID
#                             (inbound is configured above)
#   Post-MVP (Finance)        RAZORPAY_KEY_ID, RAZORPAY_SECRET,
#                             RAZORPAY_WEBHOOK_SECRET
#   Post-MVP (Platform)       RESEND_API_KEY
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# ── Monitoring (G-053) ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────
#
# Where an operational alert is delivered: any endpoint accepting a JSON POST —
# a Slack incoming webhook, a PagerDuty events URL, an internal receiver.
#
# Optional, and the consequence of leaving it unset is worth knowing: alerting
# does not become inert, it becomes local. The situation is still written to
# the log at error level, once per situation rather than every minute. What is
# lost is the part that reaches a person who is not looking.
ALERT_WEBHOOK_URL=
